WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460 align:start position:0%
 
Oh  the universe is unfathomably huge it's  so huge that it would take somewhere  around 70,000 years just to reach our  nearest neighboring star Proxima  Centauri which sits just 4.24  light-years away when you consider how  long it would take us to make that  relatively short trip it really helps to  show just how unreachable the farthest  points of space are measures not in tens  of light-years or hundreds or thousands  not even millions but distance is  measured in billions and billions of  light-years the unknown depths of space  are far beyond the reach of our current  technology so it stands to reason that  there are scores of discoveries just  waiting to be made out among the stars  one such potential discovery could  rewrite the laws of physics as we know  them if you've seen the show Rick and  Morty you're familiar with the idea of  multiple universes existing at the same  time scientists may have recently  discovered evidence for just that but  before we get started and speaking of  Rick and Morty I want to thank kwid for  sponsoring this video  Quaid is a new free app for iOS and  Android that lets you collect exclusive  stickers cards and figures right from  your phone use a lot of emojis when you  text your friends quit has thousands of  unique stickers that you can't find  anywhere else with sets from games like  fallout and five nights at freddys and  from shows like Game of Thrones Breaking  Bad Adventure Time and of course Rick  and Morty with QuIDD you can meet new  people trade stickers compare  collections and easily drag and drop  stickers into text messages opening  packs of stickers really brings me back  to the days of tearing into a new pack  of Pokemon cards as a kid and it's  seriously a lot of fun to build a  collection I personally find quit  tremendously useful when I need to  explain to somebody that their being a  Morty quit is available for iOS and the  beta version for Android to check out  the link in the description below to  download quit for free today now on with  the show this is a map of what's called  the cosmic microwave background or CMB  which is light that formed very early in  the life of our universe just 370  thousand years after the Big Bang the  blue and red dots represent minut  variations in temperature and therefore  density within the CMB indicating the  eventual birth of galaxies or empty  voids of space in 2004 astronomers  discovered something very strange  one of these cold spots located in the  constellation arisen as' is nearly a  hundred times cooler than the others and  much larger covering an expanse one  thousand times larger than the Milky Way  this spot was originally thought to be  an optical illusion caused by gravity  and a large void affecting light in the  foreground in 2015 when researchers from  the University of Hawaii attempted to  find evidence for such a void they came  away with the conclusion that there was  perhaps a small one but nothing  significant enough to explain the cold  spot according to Tom shanks of the  University of Durham  if this giant cold spot is not some  statistical fluctuation then the next  most standard explanation would be the  bubble universe collision hypothesis  this hypothesis suggests that our  universe and many others exist  simultaneously in a multi-dimensional  space like individual bubbles in a glass  of champagne every once in a while two  of these universes can collide with each  other sending a wave of energy through  our universe which would leave a  noticeable temperature bruise on the CMB  Mathew Cleavon an astronomer at NYU has  created detailed predictions of these  collisions and says if you had something  like one of these cosmic weeks which is  a kind of ripple that cuts across the  universe at that time you'll see a  particular pattern in the sky and he  suspects that this pattern would look  something like the mysterious cold spot  if the cold spot does turn out to be  solid evidence for a collision with  another universe what would that mean  one of the most important changes would  be the fact that we could possibly never  reach the ultimate goal of physics to  explain why the universe is the way it  is  if the multiverse is real then all of  our understanding of physics the speed  of light the strength of gravity  everything is arbitrary the universe  that collided with ours could operate  under an entirely different set of  physical laws every single possible  combination of variables would exist  somewhere in some other universe  floating in excessively in our bizarre  champagne glass to some people this may  seem depressing and might look like it  defeats the purpose of pursuing the  field of physics while it's true that  the existence of a multiverse would  render most of our scientific  understanding obsolete we have to  remember that Nature doesn't care about  our goals or aspirations humans have  existed for not even a blink of an eye  on a cosmic timescale the fact that  we're even here  unable to determine some of the nature  of the universe is a miraculous thing so  while the existence of another universe  may seem like a slap in the face to our  understanding of the natural world we  can take it as a new challenge for the  next generation of scientists and  astronomers and who knows maybe over the  course of the coming years will not only  be able to prove that other universes  exist but also come to understand them  and if we're really lucky maybe one day  we'll even get to send a probe to  explore these strange new frontiers and  make discoveries that would be  impossible in our home universe with  scientists actively investigating the  cold spot we could see evidence for or  against a bubble universe collision  within a year so regardless of the  outcome hopefully we won't have long to  wait of course if there are other  universes out there there's at least one  where we've already discovered them if  you enjoyed this video make sure to  subscribe to keep up to date with the  latest content and click the little bell  next to my channel name to be notified  every time I upload a new video you can  watch my previous video by clicking here  or if you're really bored you can watch  all my videos by clicking here thanks  for watching and I'll see you in the  next video

